your vegetables and fish.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.590
Okay...

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:46.050
And now, if you'll excuse me...

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:46.900
Where are you going at this hour?

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:48.630
Where are you going at this hour?

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:49.860
That is... a secret.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:50.410
That is... a secret.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.040
That is... a secret.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.370
That is... a secret.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.830
Perhaps her "secret" involves training.

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:12.510
<i>I wonder if he's asleep already. {waki service wut?}</i>

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:30.740
No peeking, you nympho.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.830
What?! In your dreams.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:37.980
It looks like the star{s?} didn't appear.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:46.210
How should I handle this whole
 "sisters' rivalry" thing?

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.920
This all happened because the Media Club was desperate for a story, right?

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.370
Kazuki, didn't I tell you before?

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:55.010
You've always lived in your sister's shadow.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:59.370
You need to break free and do
 what <i>you</i> want to do.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.710
So you say.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:06.620
If you stay the way you are,

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:10.110
Hatsune-san won't have
 any reason to change, either.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.610
This might be your chance.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:27.960
Kazuki-chan, if you don't wake up soon, 
you'll be late. Huh?

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:50.780
<i>Hatsune's not the one 
who needs to change;  </i>I<i> am.</i>

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:07.310
And now, the event you've all been
 waiting for, the swimming tournament!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:11.500
Next up is the high-school boys' relay race!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.500
Sasakasumi Academy

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.500
Swimming Tournament

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.260
On your marks!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.760
Get set!

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:25.440
Arisaka, the swimmers for the next race
 are gathering on deck.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:29.170
Do your best. I know you can win this.

00:17:29.170 --> 00:17:32.660
No, for the sake of the swimming club,
 I <i>want</i>  you to win.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:35.150
Kazuki-oneechan, FIGHT!

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:42.440
I've never seen you looking this nervous before.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:43.950
But...

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.980
My shoulders have the shakes.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:49.560
All I can do is wish you well.

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:51.000
Best of luck.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.760
Sasakasumi Academy Swimming Tournament

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:58.690
We've now reached the final match that's been on everyone's minds.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.760
Hatsune-senpai

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.760
You look so dazzling when you swim!!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.760
Mermaid Princess

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:04.960
Thank you. Thank you very much. {And now Hatsune = Elvis}

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.490
Arisaka Hatsune-san,
 a word from you before the race?

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:13.900
I'd like to show my sister
 the disparity between our talents. {Obviously in the Sailor Moon dub sense of "talents."}

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:19.020
We'd also like a comment from the
 younger sister, Kazuki-san. If you would...

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:20.410
Y-Yes...

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.940
Eh... That...

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.370
I'll do my best...

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.490
You certainly look relaxed.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:37.410
This is all fun and games, but...

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.970
I will not lose!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:47.070
Oh boy, she'd lost the psychological battle 
before it even began.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:50.740
Yes, Kazuki-san is at a sizable disadvantage.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:53.230
We should cheer her on, 
even if nobody else does.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.060
Chihaya-san, please cover your ears.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.650
Quit being such a scaredy-cat, Kazuki!!

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:03.370
Yuuji...

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.150
Didn't you break Hatsune-san's
 record during <i>practice?!</i>

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:10.290
That's why you're sure to win
 if you compete seriously.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.370
But if you lose, you must pay the penalty...

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:16.250
...of swimming nake-!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.830
I don't need <i>that</i>  kind of motivation!

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.970
Cheap shot...

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.020
My, my. You've finally gotten over yourself?

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.390
All right, you've been waiting long enough, so let's start the final match!

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.400
On your marks!

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.150
Get set!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.240
"Mermaid Princess Hatsune-san"

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.830
Hatsune-san

00:19:56.360 --> 00:20:00.410
At the 50m turnaround point, 
Hatsune has a slight lead.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.650
<i>I want to win... against my sister.</i>

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:13.340
<i>I want to win... against my sister.</i>

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.640
<i>I want to defeat... my sister!</i>

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:16.860
<i>I want to defeat... my sister!</i>

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:21.440
We have a winner! Arisaka...

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:29.240
Man, I'm so tired...

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:32.870
Wow, that was truly a race for the ages.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:38.130
If I'd just pressured you a little more,
 I would have won.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.150
You're pure evil, you know that?

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.590
She hates to lose, doesn't she?

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:44.100
Really?

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:49.230
Well, I couldn't have outswum Kazuki-chan without a little handicap.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:53.810
I guess that means Hatsune-san 
considers you a worthy opponent.

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:56.460
So? Are you surprised?

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.260
Why should I be?

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:01.300
You've always been
 good at swimming, Kazuki.

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:03.490
We used to swim together all the time.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.350
Though you might've forgotten about it.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.330
<i>He remembers...</i>

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:13.660
<i>I started swimming because Yuuji praised me.</i>

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:18.080
<i>It's all thanks to Yuuji that I beat my sister.</i>

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:22.760
I wished you would've cheered for me,
 too, if only a little.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:27.140
I totally did! I was cheering for the both of you.

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:31.820
In the depths of my heart,
 you were the only one I supported. Really!

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:30.360
Yuuji... the photos...

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:38.880
Hatsune-san, you were unbelievably cute in that swimsuit of yours. I mean it!

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:38.400
Yuuji-kun...

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:45.500
I'm ditching <i>this</i>  and going on ahead.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.640
K-Kazuki?

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:48.550
Kazuki-oneechan!

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.910
Oh, my...

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:52.720
Hmm?

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:57.560
Oh my...

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:14.890
The first time we met was on that sunlit veranda... {fi, link}

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:14.890
Hajimete deatta hidamari no BERANDA

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:20.520
Do you remember that place? {video fi, fo}

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:20.520
Oboeteru kono basho?

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:31.740
Spending time together was like breathing air, {sc, sc}

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:31.740
Maru de kuuki no you na futari no jikan

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:38.540
and we didn't realize the beauty of that placid time. {fo? or sc}

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:38.540
SUTEKI na koto kizukanai PLACID TIME

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:46.050
Our feelings of missing each other gave birth to... {sc, link}

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:46.050
Aitai kimochi kara umareta

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:50.680
...the dreams that bloomed in our hearts, {link, link}

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:50.680
Kokoro ni saku yume wo

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:56.310
which became more and more colorful. {link, link}

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:56.310
Nan domo irozuiteku dakara

00:22:56.310 --> 00:23:03.520
Will you let me stay by your side? {link, link}

00:22:56.310 --> 00:23:03.520
Anata no tonari ni isasete ne

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:07.900
I hope our silhouettes... {link, link}

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:07.900
Futatsu no SHIRUETTO

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:19.790
...will continue this endless story tomorrow. {link, fo}

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:19.790
Ashita mo tsuzuku to ii na endless story

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.320
Next Episode

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:29.440
Ever since the swimming tournament, I've been famous or something.

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:30.520
What's wrong with <i>that?</i>

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:33.530
But Yuuji scolded me and told me
 not to get carried away.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:39.970
Jealousy,

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:39.970
Perhaps?

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:36.760
Oh, I get it. That's because of "that."

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:40.020
Next on Tonagura: Jealousy, Perhaps?
